// forge with a frontend in fire (docs/ROADMAP_C_PORT.md, Phase D step 8): the command line goes unchanged to the compiler of the package forge, which runs in
// this program (libforge, linked in) - what it writes is this program's output, its exit code this program's. forge builds it for any target it builds for:
//
//   forge build tools/forge.fire --engine native -t <target> -o forge     (Windows: -t windows -o forge.exe; tcc, MinGW, ... with --toolchain)
//   forge build tools/forge.fire --engine vm -o forge                     (the VM with the program behind it)
//
// Next to the program forge finds its folders as forge-c does: FIRE_TABLES, FIRE_PACKAGES, FIRE_NATIVE_ROOT, else native/tables, Packages/ and native/ of a
// distribution (`forge package-dist`) next to it. So fire builds itself for other platforms: `forge build tools/forge.fire --engine native -t <target>`.
#import "forge"

terminate(Forge.Compiler.Main(Environment.Args))
